+# smallpt — the browser edition
+
+Kevin Beason’s [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer compiled to WebAssembly. Open `index.html` through your existing static web host. All rendering happens locally in a dedicated module Web Worker; no backend, cross-origin isolation, or third-party runtime library is needed. The checked-in `assets/smallpt.js` and `assets/smallpt.wasm` are ready to serve.
+
+The page automatically renders the original Cornell box. **Randomize colors** changes the two foreground spheres and the two walls (also spheres in smallpt), then starts a new render. **Reset** restores the original colors. Resolution and sample controls restart the render. **Save image** exports the current canvas as a PNG. The author’s reference image is shown during initialization and replaced by the first computed sample pass.
+
+## Rebuild
+
+Install and activate Emscripten 4.0.19 with emsdk, then run:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+Alternatively set `EMXX` to the absolute path of `em++`. The build compiles C++ with optimization and link-time optimization, generates the ES module and Wasm binary, and copies the static application to `dist/`. It does not launch a server.
+
+## Source and license
+
+- `vendor/smallpt.cpp`: unmodified upstream renderer.
+- `vendor/LICENSE.txt`: Kevin Beason’s MIT license.
+- `src/smallpt.cpp`: browser adaptation, retaining the original camera, scene, ray intersections, radiance, BRDFs, Russian roulette, and tent-filtered 2×2 sampling. Replaces the command-line PPM output and OpenMP loop with exported initialization, color updates, row batches, and progressive RGBA accumulation.
+- `worker.js`: initializes the Emscripten module and transfers each rendered sample pass to the page.
+- `assets/reference.png`: original author’s 25k-sample reference render from the smallpt distribution.
+
+Each rerender terminates the previous worker, freeing its Wasm heap. The module has a 1 MB stack for the recursive path tracer. Browser verification was intentionally omitted; no preview server is required by the build.
